    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T01:00:47Z",
    "body": "Correction. I wrote in this issue that `--minimized` works. That is not correct when a project is opened.\n\n`camcraft-ui --minimized <project>.camproj` stops with exit code 101 about 1.7 seconds after the start, when the project has loaded.\n\nCause: a minimized window has no area, so egui lays out a default 10000 x 10000 point screen. The viewport then asks wgpu for a 3D target of 15195 x 24595 pixels. The GPU limit on my machine is 8192, and wgpu stops the program with a validation error.\n\nThese cases do not stop: `--minimized` without a project, a running window that the user minimizes by hand, and `--no-activate`.\n\nI found this when I tested with a real project. A fix is in progress on the branch of the pull request. I will update the pull request when it is ready.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
